      {
        "n": "NTS Guide to: Obscure",
        "s": "2026-11-22T18:00:00Z",
        "e": "2026-11-22T20:00:00Z",
        "d": "For a brief period in the latter half of the '70s, Brian Eno's Obscure label made space for experimental records that sat beyond the boundaries of classical, electronic and popular music. It's brief but diverse catalogue brought together composers including Harold Budd, John Cage, Gavin Bryars, Michael Nymaan and John Adams: with release built around reptition, unusual instrumentation and found sound. \nThis episode of The NTS Guide To moves from Bryars' slowly unfolding works and Eno's own tape-loops in Discreet Music to Harold Budd's hovering piano melodies. The mood shifts between the devotional and the playful, with an overarching theme of composition that will reward the patient listener. ",
        "j": "Obscure",
        "u": "https://www.nts.live/api/v2/shows/the-nts-guide-to/episodes/the-nts-guide-to-obscure-22nd-november-2026",
        "t": "weekly"
